Spec: Control-plane mutual TLS device identity

Purpose:
  Bind actual control connections to an owner-approved P-256 device key without accepting self-reported identity.

Owns:
  ./identity.go
  ./identity_test.go

Must:
  Use standard Go TLS/x509 with a sole explicitly supplied owner root, fixed device DNS name, both EKUs, non-CA P-256 leaf and matching private key.
  Require verified client certificates and recheck current device admission after the actual handshake; disable session tickets and require TLS `1.2` or newer.
  Validate expected server key and normal chain/name checks together; never use insecure-skip verification or remote key discovery.
  Keep device-role checks outside untrusted request fields and verify wrong roots, unapproved devices and key substitutions before application delivery.
